{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,ast,hashlib,time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.load(open('/workspace/runtime_view.json'));c=r['context'];p=c['protocol']\ncommon=[\n 'Frozen data identity 9f110bfc2f037f36e2f48787b812df640fe5df2de1cda8db7ac04590c1c9be44, official split and official_offline history visibility; exactly the authorized 100-event prefix and four tasks.',\n 'One pass, batch 8192, host seed 20262027, BF16/TF32-off, dense AdamW and embedding Adagrad, sum of four BCEs, loading/scoring and all host resource accounting.',\n 'Embedding tables, target-relation/temporal core, all trainable modules and constructor/reset order, zero-initialized residual output, eight disjoint old/recent x category/brand groups, raw fractions/counts, count weight n/(n+4), shrinkage strength 4 and user centering.',\n 'Both background references and event covariance computed in every arm; identical operation shapes and trainable capacity. No added context projection from round 12.'\n]\nstudy={\n 'id':'g2-t001-slot-excluded-background-factorial',\n 'protocol_ref':r['required_study_protocol_ref'],\n 'evidence_refs':[\n  'baseline-din','g0-r0003-relation_content_counts','g2-r0004-count_shrink',\n  'g2-r0006-relation_count','g2-r0006-replicas_count',\n  'g2-r0007-aligned_early_count','g2-r0007-aligned_late_count',\n  'g2-r0008-residual_count','g2-r0008-residual_fixed','g2-r0008-residual_content',\n  'g2-r0009-joint_count','g2-r0009-product_count',\n  'g2-r0010-direct_count','g2-r0010-raw_count',\n  'g2-r0011-center_count','g2-r0011-center_fixed','g2-r0011-absolute_count',\n  'g2-r0012-context_cross_count','g2-r0012-context_add_count',\n  'paper:din','unirank-benchmark-v2','unirank-code:HiFormer'\n ],\n 'question':(\n  'Can replacing the self-inclusive feedback background with the same visible prefix excluding the current slot improve the centered relation-content/count-shrinkage model beyond g2-r0011-center_count and both frozen source bests, at matched parameters and measured cost? Does any benefit require within-slot event-feedback covariance, or is a centered mean-product sufficient?'),\n 'hypothesis':(\n  'Observed implementation limitation: g2-r0011-center_count uses each slot in its own smoothing and centering reference. For nonempty slot s with occupancy n and total N, r_s-b_user = (1-n/N)*(r_s-b_outside) when N>n. Thus self-inclusion attenuates the between-slot feedback contrast, particularly for dominant slots. This is a source-code/algebra observation; the dataset prevalence and predictive importance of dominant slots have not been measured. In exact arithmetic the current centered joint channel is alpha*[Cov_s(Wx,y)+mu_s*(r_s-b_user)], alpha=n/(n+4). Replacing b_user with b_outside in BOTH smoothing and centering selectively restores the between-slot term while leaving covariance and raw fractions unchanged. Hypothesis: this can expose useful target-relation feedback differences with no added capacity. The outside reference is a disjoint same-user event set, NOT an independent prior, mature online feedback estimate, calibrated uncertainty, or causal counterfactual. It may instead amplify noise. All four new arms fix count weighting and user centering; a background-reference x joint/factorized factorial identifies whether covariance contributes to any gain. Originality remains unverified.'),\n 'nearest_work':[\n  {'source_ref':'g2-r0011-center_count','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':\n   'candidate.py initially matched the incumbent source SHA256 06cd879a5619936c12858a8eac8d8db5937aca08be72c412a2f00adda4bcccba. Preserve its entire trainable architecture and raw statistics; replace only the background reference, with an orthogonal covariance multiplier control. The inclusive_joint arm is a calibration rerun of the parent, not an independent seed.'},\n  {'source_ref':'g0-r0003-relation_content_counts','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':\n   'Inherit target-relation content, explicit relation counts, temporal grouping, DIN bypass, static fields, one joint interaction block and four towers. Entry macro AUC 0.8275704845768582; proposed change is confined to the later feedback residual. Shared forward core, JointBlock and temporal/relation masks were checked AST-identical to this source.'},\n  {'source_ref':'g2-r0004-count_shrink','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':\n   'Inherit the conceptual n/(n+4) feedback smoothing and eight disjoint category/brand x ordinal-recency groups. Source has inclusive-user smoothing in a different compressed model (macro AUC 0.8272805336635536). Do not graft its original architecture or compare its faster runtime as a matched mechanism contrast. Here the reference excludes a slot and enters both smoothing and centering of the existing residual.'},\n  {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':\n   'Archived primary text inspected (text SHA256 83fb9eeca31e2fa3c557b6f08b893ad0018cefb33da6e00952136b9ce17e607e), including target-conditioned history pooling and Dice. These remain inherited core components. The intervention concerns an explicit masked-feedback background in a separate residual, not a new DIN activation or an exact original-paper reproduction.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:HiFormer','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':\n   'Pinned benchmark source 90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d inspected, especially lines 113-201: target pooling, field/task tokenization and interaction blocks. Current intervention is a fixed same-prefix feedback-reference replacement after an inherited relation-content core, not HiFormer tokenization or task-token readout. Benchmark section 2.3 also read. Original HiFormer detailed text is unavailable through the authorized reference and returns the benchmark fallback; no original-method equivalence or priority claim.'}\n ],\n 'inherited_components':[\n  'All 32,964,809 expected parameters of g2-r0011-center_count: 31,793,216 embedding and 1,171,593 dense; host must remeasure. No new modules, parameters, buffers, random draws, loss, or optimizer choices.',\n  'Frozen six item fields plus historical action embedding, categorical user/context fields, four historical task masks intersected with validity, input sanitation, unknown current action, zero-padding match exclusions and zero residual for empty history.',\n  'Eight disjoint groups, last 16 PREFIX POSITIONS as the recent band, uniform slot moments, bias-free 8D feedback projection, FP32 covariance accumulation, raw local feedback fractions and counts, and zero-initialized 64-hidden residual MLP.',\n  'Mechanism lineage: direct/token-aligned fusion underperformed (rounds 6-7); residual fusion improved (round 8); covariance and centering gave only small single-seed changes (rounds 9 and 11); smoothing the directly exposed fractions hurt (round 10); added static context interaction did not improve the incumbent (round 12). No failed executions are reported in the supplied trajectory; negative scientific outcomes are retained.'\n ],\n 'proposed_difference':(\n  'Implement _feedback_background from FP32 integer-valued masked task sums BEFORE division into fractions. Compute inclusive b_user=sum(y)/max(N,1) and complementary b_minus_s=(sum(y)-sum_s(y))/max(N-n_s,1). Where N=n_s, fall back to b_user; for an entirely empty prefix both are zero. Select complement or inclusive via a scalar switch after computing both. Use the chosen [B,8,4] background consistently in the inherited smoothed gate and centering offset. Cross this reference with moment_mode joint versus factorized; all arms still compute covariance, with only its scalar multiplier varying. Centered joint is approximately alpha*(J_s-mu_s*b); centered factorized is approximately alpha*mu_s*(r_s-b), allowing BF16 mean/projection rounding. Exclusion introduces no new information: it is a deterministic re-expression of authorized slot/global statistics and selective occupancy-dependent scaling of the between-slot term, NOT blanket rescaling of covariance. Raw fractions stay unsmoothed. Candidate and all controls are standalone modules with AST-identical executable structure outside literal CONFIG. No context modules from round 12 are retained.'),\n 'predictions':[\n  'Primary predictive prediction: exclude_joint has higher full-validation four-task macro AUC than inclusive_joint and the archived incumbent 0.8280959704981011, and exceeds both imported source bests 0.8275704845768582 and 0.8272805336635536. This is untested. Select by the frozen equal-weight macro AUC, then macro Logloss, parameters and trial ID; report all four AUC/Logloss changes against baseline-din, both sources and incumbent without a new task veto.',\n  'Mechanistic predictions before training: with no outside events, inclusive and excluded features coincide; empty slots remain zero; with equal feedback rates inside/outside the background switch has no effect; otherwise exclusion changes only the between-slot component and preserves alpha*covariance. In exact arithmetic joint-minus-factorized equals alpha*covariance under either background. A same-marginal different-pairing synthetic contrast affects the covariance path, while the reference intervention acts through slot/global feedback counts.',\n  'Interpret the factorial using delta_bg_joint=AUC(exclude_joint)-AUC(inclusive_joint), delta_bg_factorized=AUC(exclude_factorized)-AUC(inclusive_factorized), and their difference. Positive background effects in both moment modes support utility of the reference transformation but do not require covariance. A positive interaction and a positive joint-versus-factorized contrast would provisionally support complementary joint-event content. No single run establishes a mechanism.',\n  'Use the host-available predeclared empty/1-16/17-64/>64 history-length slices with sample, positive and negative counts